          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "content": "Architecture",
            "variant": "h3",
            "align": "left",
            "color": "foreground",
            "transform": "none"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_th_stack_body",
          "layout": {
            "col": 1,
            "colSpan": 12,
            "row": 5,
            "rowSpan": 12
          },
          "mobile": {
            "layout": {
              "rowSpan": 18
            }
          },
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "content": "Originally, Thang had a RESTful Next.js / Node.js backend with MongoDB underneath. Its Identity flew through Firebase Auth and the backend lived on Vercel. This architecture prepared the game for more competitive settings allowing matchmaking and hosting dedicated servers. However, this was simply too much for an indie party game, so I had to find a cheaper alternative. We pivoted back to P2P and simplified networking stack into EOS. This allows us to keep the maintenance cost of the game to be $0. ",
            "variant": "body",
            "align": "left",
            "color": "foreground",
            "transform": "none"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
